        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "50433f51-53ef-3dc6-acbe-1bb30a2a980b",
                "word": "désapprobation",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5dfab764-6420-437b-aa95-d81095ee3b81",
                        "entry_id": "50433f51-53ef-3dc6-acbe-1bb30a2a980b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "désapprobations"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f31fb423-6f73-3396-8d65-f3ec51acb651",
                        "entry_id": "50433f51-53ef-3dc6-acbe-1bb30a2a980b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Action de désapprouver."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d1f00bd-ae33-45d9-ba7c-02a7cd511348",
                                "sense_id": "f31fb423-6f73-3396-8d65-f3ec51acb651",
                                "text": "Ah ! messieurs, vous prenez vite pied chez nous ! Vous êtes de mauvaise humeur parce que je n’ai pas été assez sot pour signer, comme Louis XIV, la désapprobation des libertés gallicanes !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2dbc673d-e2ae-490a-8743-8442c5d631b0",
                                "sense_id": "f31fb423-6f73-3396-8d65-f3ec51acb651",
                                "text": "– Bien, fit-elle, alors, vous allez comprendre à merveille. Mais que je ne voie pas dans vos regards la moindre nuance de désapprobation. Je m’arrêterais à l’instant même."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ade96099-4964-4992-8cdf-792e8cc8992a",
                                "sense_id": "f31fb423-6f73-3396-8d65-f3ec51acb651",
                                "text": "Au troisième stade, la tension pouvait aller jusqu’à la désapprobation verbale ou, partiellement verbalisée."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "39ed4c7a-9034-4f9d-8b49-f4b9e866a3fe",
                        "source_entry_id": "50433f51-53ef-3dc6-acbe-1bb30a2a980b",
                        "source_sense_id": "f31fb423-6f73-3396-8d65-f3ec51acb651",
                        "target_lang_word": "disapproval",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disapproval",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3460ec08-2cc7-3699-9b97-cac5d484ceeb",
                                        "entry_id": "1a8c25f6-a73a-38e2-a0d1-822dff5e1cfd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of disapproving; condemnation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a56e46d-87a0-403c-ad1e-4a72f669a484",
                                                "sense_id": "3460ec08-2cc7-3699-9b97-cac5d484ceeb",
                                                "text": "Everyone glared in disapproval at the man talking loudly on the phone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f67a5ef0-2568-4af7-9242-133805582a39",
                        "source_entry_id": "50433f51-53ef-3dc6-acbe-1bb30a2a980b",
                        "source_sense_id": "f31fb423-6f73-3396-8d65-f3ec51acb651",
                        "target_lang_word": "disapprobation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "disapprobation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "945539df-5e41-3ba4-baf7-0ad0c74d7e54",
                                        "entry_id": "a26aef64-cd17-3c97-9bdd-f0d8ec6af651",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act or expression of condemnation or disapproval, especially on moral grounds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0be1fd2-fea8-41d2-95d1-d1d37e9ba3aa",
                                                "sense_id": "945539df-5e41-3ba4-baf7-0ad0c74d7e54",
                                                "text": "Though a gentle Sigh which ſtole from the Boſom of Nancy, ſeemed to argue ſome ſecret Diſapprobation of theſe Sentiments, ſhe did not dare openly to oppoſe them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "977d5990-9b0d-4f82-bf1f-009df41e9f0b",
                                                "sense_id": "945539df-5e41-3ba4-baf7-0ad0c74d7e54",
                                                "text": "Elizabeth would wonder, and probably would blame her; and though her resolution was not to be shaken, her feelings must be hurt by such disapprobation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1bd194e-013d-4bf3-bf3a-adddc89b92e6",
                                                "sense_id": "945539df-5e41-3ba4-baf7-0ad0c74d7e54",
                                                "text": "Believe me, I have no warmer sentiment to bestow; and even if I had I could not indulge it, since it would meet with the decided disapprobation of my family, and never could I bring myself to act in opposition to them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22ab7b8a-cb3c-4147-8c05-7255ffe1b3a1",
                                                "sense_id": "945539df-5e41-3ba4-baf7-0ad0c74d7e54",
                                                "text": "And not only these acts, but the dispositions which lead to them, are properly immoral, and fit subjects of disapprobation which may rise to abhorrence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d7a5755-c011-4e28-915d-66014d8e1a7d",
                                                "sense_id": "945539df-5e41-3ba4-baf7-0ad0c74d7e54",
                                                "text": "No one seems to think so, however. Yet they view my arrival with a knapsack on my back with cold disapprobation, as unseemly as if I had arrived riding on a pig. I ought to be in a carriage, and the knapsack ought to be a new suitcase."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e829fc4b-d01d-4cb1-98dc-bac0bf846cfc",
                        "source_entry_id": "50433f51-53ef-3dc6-acbe-1bb30a2a980b",
                        "source_sense_id": "f31fb423-6f73-3396-8d65-f3ec51acb651",
